host file share: Mac photos and videos to the app's own share targets (Arquivo menu, drop on the window, the app's create button), and the Edit menu

A file chosen from the menu bar (Arquivo) or dropped on the window is started on
one of the app's share targets as ACTION_SEND / ACTION_SEND_MULTIPLE, which is
what another app's share sheet does on a device. Finder drags arrive as file
URLs, Photos drags as file promises (NSFilePromiseReceiver); a drop asks for the
destination with a menu where the files landed, opened after the drop has been
answered so the drag's source is not kept waiting.

MACAPK_HOST_CLICK="id/<entry name>=<target>" hands a click on the app's own view
to the same file panel (View.performClick -> DocumentPickerHandler.macapkHostPick).
Instamac sets it for the main feed's create button, whose own screen (the camera
page) this runtime does not show. The first panel of a run opens on Pictures.
The embedded Info.plist lists the localizations, so the panel is drawn in the
user's language instead of English.

The guest never opens the user's originals. document_picker.mm stages each file
under the temporary directory on a background queue (an APFS clone, or a JPEG
re-encode in sRGB for HEIC / TIFF / RAW), batches older than a day are swept, and
the staged copies are served through HostDocumentsProvider with a read grant,
like a picked document. DocumentPickerHandler.macapkOnHostShare builds the Intent
(EXTRA_STREAM plus the ClipData that carries the grant) and delivers it on the
cross-app arrival path with DocumentsUI as the sender.

PackageManager.resolveContentProvider answers for the ExternalStorageProvider
authority the host documents carry: another package under another uid, as on a
device. Instagram 455's direct share target refuses a content:// URI whose
provider resolves to nothing or to its own uid (it showed a toast and finished);
with this it opens its recipient sheet.

The Edit menu (cut / copy / paste / select all / emoji) and its responder
actions are in the same cocoa_bridge.mm hunks; the menu block supersedes the one
published in 0015. The hostkey harness gains "share <target> <path>[|<path>]".

Measured on Instagram 455 (macOS 27.2): one JPEG to the feed target reaches the
editor and the "new post" screen; JPEG + HEIC as SEND_MULTIPLE reach the editor
(HEIC staged as JPEG); the direct target opens the recipient list. The story target opens
the story editor with the photo (after 0023). A tap on the feed's create button opens the panel on
Pictures. Cmd+V with a 37-character string on a test pasteboard lands in the
caption field of the "new post" screen.

